lection polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Mississippi remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential elections, with a partisan lean of roughly eleven points toward the GOP and recent Republican wins by wide margins. The 2028 contest is an open race, since the incumbent president is term-limited, and neither party has settled on a nominee.\n\nNo Mississippi-specific general-election polls, expert ratings, or fundraising figures are available, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan balance. That points to a Republican advantage of about eleven points, consistent with a Likely Republican rating. Headlines about competitive 2026 races elsewhere suggest some national fluidity, but nothing yet indicates Mississippi is trending toward the Democrats. A strong Democratic national wave or early state polling showing narrowing would be the clearest sign this race is tightening.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1069, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1631, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1578, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1586, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1588, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.158, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1552, "margin": -11.0}]}